@@ -0,0 +1,82 @@
+# DEPLOY-NEXT-1 implementation plan
+
+## Boundary and result
+
+This round adds the Worker that owns the `commonplace_next` container and the o
nly outbound lane
+available to it. It does not change `Dockerfile`, `config/`, `lib/`, the Cloudf
lare Access
+application, or the five production boot requirements. The container therefore
continues to use
+`http://storage.internal`; `COMMONPLACE_SIDECAR_URL` is not one of its deployed
 environment
+variables.
+
+`CommonplaceNextContainer` listens on port 4000, sleeps after ten minutes, and
has
+`enableInternet = false`. Its environment contains exactly the five values prod
uction already
+requires:
+
+* `SECRET_KEY_BASE`
+* `COMMONPLACE_ACCESS_ISSUER`
+* `COMMONPLACE_ACCESS_AUDIENCE`
+* `COMMONPLACE_ACCESS_JWKS_URI`
+* `COMMONPLACE_ACCESS_ROSTER`
+
+The Worker additionally reads `COMMONPLACE_LOG_REALM_URL` and the secret
+`COMMONPLACE_LOG_REALM_CAPABILITY`. Those two bindings are never copied into `e
nvVars`, so the
+container process cannot read either one.
+
+## Lane and authority
+
+`CommonplaceNextContainer.outboundByHost` registers only `storage.internal`. Th
e handler checks
+the request hostname before reading bindings or invoking a transport. It reject
s every other host
+with 403. For the accepted host it retains the path and query, resolves them ag
ainst
+`COMMONPLACE_LOG_REALM_URL`, deletes any `authorization` supplied by the contai
ner, then installs
+`Authorization: Bearer <COMMONPLACE_LOG_REALM_CAPABILITY>`. The realm endpoint
must be HTTPS and
+all binding or transport failures return a generic response without logging req
uest details.
+The entry module exports the SDK's `ContainerProxy`, which is the runtime targe
t for intercepted
+egress.
+
+This bearer capability is strictly weaker than the log Worker lane's platform-s
upplied
+`ctx.containerId` authority. The compensating boundary is explicit: the credent
ial exists only as
+a Worker secret; the process cannot read it; and an offline container can reach
 only the registered
+store lane. A compromised process can use its store authority through that lane
, but cannot select
+another authority or exfiltrate the capability over another network path.
+
+The named repair is to package the log Worker's store implementation for both r
epositories and
+restore `ctx.containerId` as the authority. That repair is outside this round.
+
+## Deployment custody
+
+The dispatcher supplies the capability out of band. Its value must never be wri
tten to a command
+line, repository file, message, log, or response. Configure only the binding na
me
+`COMMONPLACE_LOG_REALM_CAPABILITY` through the deployment secret mechanism. Con
figure
+`COMMONPLACE_LOG_REALM_URL` and the five container values in the Worker environ
ment. Do not add
+`COMMONPLACE_SIDECAR_URL`.
+
+`wrangler deploy` builds and rolls out the configured container image. This rou
nd does not run it;
+deployment belongs to the dispatcher under a separate announced act. A local, n
on-deploying bundle
+check is:
+
+```sh
+cd worker
+npm ci
+npm test
+npm run check
+```
+
+## Arms
+
+Run A1–A4 and the structural Worker checks with `cd worker && npm test`. The su
ite injects a fake
+transport and fake capability; no real credential or network is needed. A1 incl
udes a positive
+transport control before proving that three wrong hosts return 403 with zero tr
ansport calls. A2
+starts with a container-chosen authorization value and proves that only the inj
ected secret leaves
+the lane. A3 positively finds the fake secret in that outgoing header, then pro
ves it is absent
+from captured output and both success and failure response bodies. A4 exercises
 all seven route
+paths with query strings.
+
+A5 is executable as `cd worker && bash test/a5-local-boot.sh`. It uses
+`commonplace-next:2594dc7` unless `A5_IMAGE` names another already-built image.
 First it requires a
+plain container run to fail with both `storage.internal … :nxdomain` and the Re
alm child failure.
+Then it starts the stateful seven-route stub, proves the stub is reachable, sup
plies the sidecar URL
+only to the local review container, and requires the release container to remai
n alive and answer
+HTTP. The local-only override is an arm instrument, not deployment configuratio
n.
+
+A6 is `rm -rf tmp/test-data && mix test`, after the Worker suite. No Elixir sou
rce or test is changed
+by this round.
